,{title:"Krishna School of Physiotherapy & Rehabilitation (KSPR)"}),r.jsx(vr,{dirImg:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1726717188/KPGU/Faculty%20Images/KSPR/img-0081-66eb9cdc8d9b6_yai2pg.webp",dirEmail:"dir.kspr@kpgu.ac.in",dirName:"Prof. (Dr.) Paras Bhura",dirOf:"Krishna School of Physiotherapy & Rehabilitation",dirOfShort:"[KSPR]",dirMessage:["Welcome to the Krishna School of Physiotherapy Rehabilitation (KSPR), KPGU-Vadodara, where we are dedicated to fostering multifaceted excellence in education, research, and community outreach. Our mission is to create a learning environment that not only develops skilled and compassionate physiotherapists but also drives innovation and leadership in the field of healthcare.","At KPGU, we believe in a holistic approach to education. Our curriculum is designed to blend academic rigor with hands-on clinical experience, empowering our students to excel in both practice and research. With a strong emphasis on evidence-based practice and cutting-edge research, we are shaping the future of physiotherapy to meet the ever-evolving demands of healthcare systems worldwide.","Our commitment to outreach and community engagement is integral to our identity. Through partnerships, collaborations, and service-based learning, we ensure our students understand the real-world impact of their knowledge, making a positive difference in the lives of individuals and communities. Our faculty, distinguished for their expertise and dedication, are passionate about guiding students toward academic and professional success.","As a forward-thinking institution, we continuously strive to push the boundaries of healthcare education and research. I invite you to explore the unique opportunities we offer at KPGU and become part of a community that is not only shaping the future of physiotherapy but also contributing to a healthier, more equitable world."]})]})}),r.jsx("div",{style:{padding:"40px 0 0 0"},id:"vision",children:r.jsxs(w,{bgcolo