s) at Drs. Kiran & Pallavi Patel Global University (KPGU), Vadodara to make the present education system inclusive, to become more responsive to the needs and constraints of the disabled social groups. EOC shall make ensure that students, staffs, faculties or the community from various diverse backgrounds, caste, creed, religion, language, ethnicity, gender and disability are not deprived of their righteous opportunities in terms of providing equity, free from any form of harassment, opportunities to higher educational institution, free from ragging, unfavorable treatment and victimization. The University aims to provide equal opportunities among the community and enhance diversity within the campus."})]})}),r.jsx("div",{id:"objectives",children:r.jsxs(w,{maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgcolor:"#fff",mt:7,borderRadius:4,className:"smooth-shadow",textAlign:{xs:"start",sm:"justify"},children:[r.jsx("h3",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary ",children:"Objectives of Equal Opportunity Cell"}),r.jsxs(w,{m:1,children:[r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To safeguard the interest of the students without any prejudice to their caste, creed, religion, language, ethnicity, gender and disability."}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To eliminate discrimination against or harassment by prohibiting it and by providing preventive and protective measures to facilitate its eradication and punishments."}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To promote equality among students of all sections of the society."}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To provide Equal Opportunity for all and not to discriminate against students belonging to SC and ST in admission."}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To resolve the issues pertaining to caste, creed, religion, language, ethnicity, gender and disability of access etamong the students staff & faculties."}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To provide a platform for listening to complaints and redressal of grievances, if any"}),r.jsx("h5",{className:"mb-2 p-2 smooth-shadow-card rounded-2 color-secondary fw-bold ",children:"To foster healthy relationship with all."})]})]})}),r.jsx("div",{id:"committee",children:r.jsxs(w,{maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgcolor:"#fff",mt:7,borderRadius:4,className:"smooth-shadow",textAlign:{xs:"start",sm:"justify"},children:[r.jsx("h3",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary mb-4",children:"Members of Anti-Discrimination Committee"}),r.jsxs(jn,{elevation:0,className:"smooth-shadow-card",children:[r.jsx(En,{expandIcon:r.jsx(zn,{}),"aria-controls":"panel1-content",id:"panel1-header",children:r.jsx("h3",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary",children:"Composition of Committees for Ragging Prevention and Response"})}),r.jsx(Pn,{children:r.jsxs("table",{style:{width:"100%"},children:[r.jsxs("thead",{style:{},className:"text-white",children:[r.jsxs("th",{className:"p-2 fs-5 border-5 border-white  text-uppercase",style:{letterSpacing:"1px",background:"#264796",borderRadius:"10px"},children:["Name"," "]}),r.jsxs("th",{className:"p-2 fs-5 border-5 border-white  text-uppercase",style:{letterSpacing:"1px",background:"#264796",borderRadius:"10px"},children:["Designation"," "]}),r.jsx("th",{className:"p-2 fs-5 border-5 border-white  text-uppercase",style:{letterSpacing:"1px",background:"#264796",borderRadius:"10px"},children:"Email Id"})]}),r.jsx("tbody",{children:i.map(({Name:s,Designation:l,Email:c},d)=>r.jsx(o,{Name:s,Designation:l,Email:c},d))})]})})]})]})}),r.jsx("div",{id:"complaint-procedure",children:r.jsxs(w,{maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgcolor:"#fff",mt:7,borderRadius:4,className:"smooth-shadow",textAlign:{xs:"start",sm:"justify"},children:[r.jsx("h3",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary ",children:"Complaint Procedure"}),r.jsxs("h5",{className:"fw-bold mb-4",children:["An aggrieved person (who has been victimized) may launch the complaints by Sending an email to ",r.jsx("br",{}),r.jsx($,{variant:"contained",color:"secondary",href:"mailto:eoc@kpgu.ac.in",size:"small",className:"text-lowercase mt-2",children:"eoc@kpgu.ac.in"})]}),r.jsxs(ao,{color:"warning",icon:r.jsx(Ml,{}),children:[r.jsx("h5",{className:"fw-bold mb-3 ",children:"Note"}),r.jsxs("ol",{children:[r.jsx("li",{className:"fw-bold fs-6",children:"Submit the complaint within one months from the date of the incident and in case of a series of incidents within a period of one months from the date of the last incident."}),r.jsx("li",{className:"fw-bold fs-6",children:"You have to mention all your details like name, designation, mobile no & mail Id, Enrolment no in case of students, staffs & faculties."}),r.jsx("li",{className:"fw-bold fs-6",children:"Mention the incident description like date, time, location, respondent’s name, working relationships etc."}),r.jsx("li",{className:"fw-bold fs-6",children:"Committee shall follow the KPGU policy on prevention of discriminations among all."})]})]})]})}),r.jsx("div",{id:"contact"}),r.jsxs(w,{maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgcolor:"#fff",mt:7,borderRadius:4,className:"smooth-shadow",textAlign:{xs:"start",sm:"justify"},children:[r.jsx("h3",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary ",children:"Contact Us"}),r.jsxs("address",{className:"fw-bold",children:["Anti discrimination Committee",r.jsx("br",{}),"Drs. Kiran & Pallavi Patel Global University",r.jsx("br",{}),"Vadodara, 391240",r.jsx("br",{}),"Gujarat",r.jsx("br",{}),r.jsx($,{variant:"contained",color:"secondary",href:"mailto:eoc@kpgu.ac.in",size:"small",className:"text-lowercase mt-2",children:"eoc@kpgu.ac.in"})]})]})]})}function Vre(){const{maxWidth:e}=p.useContext(X),t=xt(),n=[{center:"Krishna Centre of Innovation Research (KCIR)",des:"Krishna Centre for Research and Innovation fosters cutting-edge research aligned with societal, national, and global issues, aiming to enhance India's competitiveness. It promotes interdisciplinary collaboration, provides funding, and ensures quality standards.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-centre-of-innovation-research"},{center:"Krishna Center of Institutional Social Responsibility (KCISR)",des:"Krishna Center of Institutional Social Responsibility (KCISR), focuses on social welfare initiatives. It engages students and employees, emphasizing areas like environment, community, and research-driven solutions for societal advancement.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-center-of-institution-social-responsibility"},{center:"Krishna Center of International Affairs (KCIA)",des:"Krishna Center of International Affairs (KCIA) established to foster global connections. Its objectives include facilitating student exchanges, supporting foreign students, promoting collaborations, and enhancing research and learning opportunities.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-center-of-international-affairs"},{center:"Krishna Center of Career Advancement Corporate Training (KCCACT)",des:"Krishna Center of Career Advancement & Corporate Training (KCCACT) aids students in exploring career options and provides counseling and training to align their skills with industry needs, fostering career growth and professional development.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-center-of-career-advancement-corporate"},{center:"Krishna Center of Startups and Entrepreneurship (KCSE)",des:"Krishna Centre of Excellence in Startup and Entrepreneurship fosters innovation and entrepreneurship, providing support to aspiring entrepreneurs. Through policy frameworks and collaboration, it aims to create a vibrant startup ecosystem, contributing to economic growth and job creation.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-center-of-startups-and-entrepreneurship"},{center:"Krishna Center of Training in Disaster Management (KCTDM)",des:"The Krishna Centre of Training in Disaster Management addresses the increasing frequency of natural and man-made disasters, aiming to minimize their impact through awareness, education, and research aligned with national guidelines.",link:"/centers-cells/krishna-center-of-training-in-disaster-management"}],a=({center:i,des:o,link:s})=>r.jsx(k,{item:!0,xs:12,sm:6,md:4,children:r.jsxs(w,{className:"smooth-shadow-card h-100",borderRadius:4,overflow:"hidden",p:2,position:"relative",children:[r.jsx("h4",{className:"fw-bold color-secondary",children:i}),r.jsx("h6",{className:"mb-5 fw-bold text-secondary",children:o}),r.jsx(ce,{position:"absolute",bottom:16,children:r.jsx($,{variant:"contained",color:"secondary",endIcon:r.jsx(ze,{}),onClick:()=>t(s),children:"view more"})})]})});return r.jsx(w,{maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgcolor:"#fff",mt:7,borderRadius:4,className:"smooth-shadow",children:r.jsx(k,{container:!0,spacing:4,children:n.map(({center:i,des:o,link:s},l)=>r.jsx(a,{center:i,des:o,link:s},l))})})}function Hre(){const{maxWidth:e}=p.useContext(X),t=[{des:"As the new and innovative career and professional prospects are developing practically every day, the “World of Work” is the need of an hour not only to sustain in career but to grow significantly in profession."},{des:"Krishna Center of Career Advancement & Corporate Training (KCCACT) is aimed to assist all university students in identifying their interests and strengths, exploring a variety of opportunities to enhance experience and clarity about their goals, and empowering them to pursue paths that are deeply relevant to them."},{des:"The policy of Career advancement aims to assist students in exploring the world of employment and new career avenues, as well as assisting students in career planning through counseling, in which they acquire information about themselves in terms of their interests, aptitudes, and abilities in order to effectively select their career. It is therefore, the process of effectively correlating a candidate’s internal psychology with external variables of employability and courses, prioritizing and selecting the best option."},{des:"Training provided at KCCACT are also important for corporate professionals seeking career advancement in their respective fields."},{des:"The goal of KCCACT is to help students realize their full potential by educating them to refine and augment their abilities, matching them with corporate standards and bringing in corporations to choose and place them. Students can largely get benefitted from the Centre of career advancement and corporate training, because it bridges the gap between their potential and their employment opportunities in India and abroad."},{des:"KCCACT has the best of in-house faculty and expert visiting faculty on its panel to provide training on functional and technical skills to develop a pool of skilled, competent, and productive professionals for contemporary India and the globe. Based on special technical and specific behavior skills needs, trainings are also provided by KCCACT to enhance the output of corporate employees working in organizations."}],n=[{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527589/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/sttp-on-effective-communication-skills-custom-66f7fa855f3d3_mqh4pm.webp",title:"STTP ON EFFECTIVE COMMUNICATION SKILLS",des:"KCCACT had  organized a Short-Term Training Program (STTP) on Effective Communication Skills on November 8th and 9th, 2023. Since communication is key to innovative teaching, it is often said that successful teaching relies 50% on knowledge and 50% on effective communication skills. 129 teaching staff benefitting out of this STTP.",date:"08-11-2023"},{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527591/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/faculty-development-program-on-machine-learning-computer-vision-iot-sap-and-abap-custom-66f7fa7f7c84b_zjbvke.webp",title:"Faculty Development Program  on  Machine Learning, Computer Vision, IOT, SAP and ABAP",des:"KCCACT had organized the 5 Days Faculty Development Program during 23-11-2023 to 28-11-2023  for CSE/IT (Degree and Diploma) Staff Members in association of Edunet foundation supported by SAP and under Code Unnati Program. The motive of the FDP was to accelerate the knowledge in various technical field and to remain up to date now days as an academician."},{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527590/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/presentation-skills-custom-66f7fa7f9b99e_jgh3xb.webp",title:"Presentation Skills",des:'KCCACT organized a seminar on "Presentation Skills" for pre-final year students from KSET, KSN, and KSS on March 21, 2023, focusing on not only academic presentations like projects and seminars but also on how to present oneself effectively in all aspects of society and the corporate world, benefiting a total of 180 students.',date:" 21/03/2023"},{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527592/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/seminar-on-reseme-building-custom-66f7fa82e5ed1_ipvcd4.webp",title:"Seminar on Resume Building",des:"The Krishna Center for Career Advancement and Corporate Training – Center of Excellence organized a seminar for final-year B.Tech/B.E. and Diploma students on October 30, 2023, aimed at equipping them with essential knowledge and skills for building an impactful resume, as it serves as a person's first impression. The seminar benefited 184 students by helping them present their qualifications, experience, and achievements clearly and compellingly to potential employers.",date:" 30/10/2023"},{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527589/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/seminar-on-learning-strategies-custom-66f7fa826d092_qiaczy.webp",title:"Seminar on Learning Strategies",des:'KCCACT had organized seminars on "Learning Strategies," covering topics such as the myths of popular learning, learning strategies, and better approaches to effective studying. Students gained insights into different learning strategies and how to study in a more structured and effective manner. Over 150 students from KSET, 100 from KAMC, 100 from KSN, and 80 from KSBM benefited from the sessions on popular learning techniques.',date:" 00/00/2023"},{img:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1727527589/KPGU/Images/Events/Krishna%20Center%20of%20Career%20Advancement%20Corporate%20Training/workshop-on-scale-up-with-skill-custom-66f7fa85a3815_gw4m6w.webp",title:"Workshop on Scale up with skill",des:'KCCACT conducted a one-week workshop titled "Scale Up with Skills" from April 2 to April 9, 2022, aimed at capacity building for non-teaching staff at KPGU University. Hosted by the Krishna School of Emerging Technology & Applied Research in Vadodara, the workshop focused on specialized technical skills and specific behaviours to enhance the productivity of non-teaching employees at KPGU University.',date:" 02/04/2022 To 09/04/2022"}],a=["To inculcate ethical values among the students to make them quality professionals.","To inspire and guide students in making wise career decisions.","To prepare students for industrial needs to grab the global opportunities.","To enhance the knowledge in all sphere of the staff for their career advancement and professional growth."],i=[{name:"Dr. Nandini M. Chaudhari",image:"https://res.cloudinary.com/dby2vbxv3/image/upload/v1709635524/KPGU/Faculty%20Images/KSET/hod-it.webp",designation:"Dy. Director, Career Advancement and Corporate Training ",quote:"It is said that “No matter your industry, role, or career objectives, knowledge is power"}],o=({name:s,img:l,designation:c,quote:d})=>r.jsxs(k,{container:!0,maxWidth:e,mx:"auto",p:"3%",bgc